  "conclusions": [
    "All 13 modes have valid complete timing, exact candidate inventory, source/runtime evidence, recorded exact repeats and restoration, and recomputed saved-output error metrics.",
    "Shared BF16 to T0 increases both complete-call latency and independently profiled GPU work even though DiT Graph kernel count decreases. Fewer kernels or lower integer precision alone does not establish a faster complete policy call.",
    "T5 to T6 wall median increases but independently profiled GPU work and DiT Graph kernel work decrease. This profile does not support a slower W4 GPU-kernel explanation for the T6 wall bump.",
    "T7 to T8 (66.7 percent) does show a modest profiled GPU-work increase and 64 more DiT Graph kernels. Causal attribution to a specific fusion requires a controlled ablation.",
    "T10 wall median is only about 0.94 percent lower than shared BF16. Ten samples in a single ordered sweep do not establish a statistically robust optimum or task quality."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Repeat and restoration exactness are verified from recorded comparison evidence; duplicate repeat/restoration arrays were not separately saved.",
